{
    "background_story": "Della was a dedicated humanitarian aid worker who spent years traveling to remote areas of the world to provide medical assistance. Before each trip, she would meticulously prepare herself, researching the local diseases and taking necessary precautions. On one such trip to a malaria-prone region, Della was prescribed mefloquine, a powerful antimalarial medication. Despite the potential side effects, she took the medication diligently, knowing it was crucial to her safety. As she worked tirelessly to set up medical clinics and treat local patients, Della's commitment to her work never wavered. Her dedication and selflessness inspired countless others to follow in her footsteps, and she became a respected leader in her field. Della's experience with mefloquine was just one aspect of her remarkable journey, but it played a vital role in keeping her safe as she changed lives around the world.",
